# Day 49/50 — Internet of Things (IoT)

Imagine your alarm ringing, your lights switching on and your coffee machine getting ready — all through connected devices.

This is the idea behind the **Internet of Things (IoT)**

IoT connects everyday physical objects to the internet, allowing them to collect and exchange data.
Smart watches, home automation systems, connected vehicles and smart city devices are some examples.

Ordinary objects become capable of sensing, communicating and responding.

It's fascinating how technology is slowly becoming part of things we once considered completely ordinary.

But it also raises questions about privacy, security and how much control we give these devices.

**Because the future isn't just about connecting more things. It's about deciding what those connections should mean.**
